{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310652,"nonce":"4B4cvDOsBlLegN0IlTNde1h9Tf8=","title":"FOUR MIR miscompiles from ONE defect class — a pass answering a whole-program question from a local scan. Fixed: GlobalLoadCaching ...","message":"A pass answers a WHOLE-PROGRAM question — can anything else write this? is this\ncall pure? — from a scan of ONE function or ONE block, then rewrites on the\nstrength of it. Every instance was a silent wrong answer with no diagnostic, at\nthe DEFAULT optimisation level, and at MIR level so every backend inherited it.\n\n| pass | defect | witness result |\n|---|---|---|\n| GlobalLoadCaching (f0235179) | \"stored to\" scanned only the loading fn, so a callee's store was invisible | one `static var` read as two storages |\n| CSE (1e98a5c9) | keyed a global load by id with NO invalidation on store or call | `c=7; a=c; c=a+1; b=c` -\u003e 14, want 15 |\n| LICM (cad615c9) | a read has no operands and no side effects, so it was hoisted even when the loop wrote it | loop sum -\u003e 0, want 15 |\n| LoopUnrolling (ea49cde1) | remapped 13 of ~64 instruction kinds, cloned the rest UNCHANGED (same dest + same operands) | `while(i\u003c4){c=c+i;i=i+1}` -\u003e 0, want 6 |\n\n`RAYZOR_DISABLE_PASSES=licm,cse,...` skips passes by name.\n**IT ONLY AFFECTS `rayzor bundle`.** `rayzor run` constructs its own\nPassManager and ignores the variable — a bisect through `run` appeared to clear\nevery pass including \"all disabled\", which is what made it look like a backend\nbug. Method that works:\n1. `bundle -O 0/1/2/3` to confirm it is optimisation-dependent.\n2. `bundle -O 2` with ALL passes disabled — if correct, it IS a MIR pass.\n3. Re-enable one at a time; the one that breaks it is the culprit.\nPass names: constant-folding control-flow-simplification copy-propagation cse\ndead-code-elimination devirtualization global_load_cache gvn licm\nloop-unrolling scalar_replacement strip-stack-trace-updates\ntail-call-optimization unreachable-block-elimination.\n\n- `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR` dumps POST-MERGE, PRE-OPTIMISATION. The MIR it prints can\n  be perfectly correct while the artifact miscompiles. It cannot clear a pass.\n- `aot -O 2` fails to build at HEAD on an unrelated LLVM verification error in\n  `_i64ToDouble`, so bisect via `bundle`, not `aot`.\n- A regression test is worthless until watched to FAIL. Three drafts of the\n  first test passed against the unfixed compiler. Reproducing needs the exact\n  shape: for the static bug, a module split + a POINTER static + both reads in\n  ONE method called twice.\n\nThe audit that found these had 11 of 25 agents die on a session limit.\nUNVERIFIED candidates remain: ScalarReplacement (malloc/free identified by\nNAME, so a user `Pool.malloc`/`free` is treated as the allocator),\nBoundsCheckElimination (`is_array_invariant` misses mutation inside a callee),\nInsertFree (`classify_func` name collision; closure-captured buffer freed at\nreturn), LoopVectorization, Devirtualization (store-to-load forwarding of a\nfunction-pointer slot), and `FunctionAttributes.pure` set from \"no branches\".\nWitnesses I wrote for purity-CSE, devirtualization-after-reassignment,\nSRA-of-an-escaping-object and LICM-around-a-for-loop all PASSED — those shapes\nare clean; the rest are untested, not cleared.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_mir_local_scan_global_conclusion` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}